## exp008 Results — Stochastic DDIM Diversity Evaluation ✅

**Setup**: Evaluation-only experiment using exp007 checkpoint with eta=0.3 and eta=0.5 stochastic DDIM sampling.

### Key Surprise: eta>0 Improves Quality (Not Just Diversity)

| Metric | η=0.0 (exp007) | η=0.3 | η=0.5 |
|--------|----------------|-------|-------|
| **Mean RPA** | 92.80% | **94.26%** ↑ | **94.01%** ↑ |
| **Oracle RPA** | 95.51% | **96.39%** ↑ | **96.13%** ↑ |
| **Amp RMSE oracle** | 0.897 | 0.807 ↑ | **0.773** ↑ |
| **VDE** | 4.84 | 4.80 | **4.78** |
| Oracle-mean gap | 2.71% | 2.13% | 2.12% |

### Main Findings:
1. **Stochastic DDIM unexpectedly improves mean quality** — η=0.3 gives the best Mean RPA at 94.26%, up from 92.80% at η=0.0
2. **Oracle-mean gap did NOT widen** — diversity was not significantly increased (gap shrank from 2.7% to ~2.1%)
3. **Amp quality improved significantly** — RMSE(log) oracle dropped from 0.897 to 0.773 at η=0.5, approaching baseline's 0.738
4. **VDE/VRE remain far superior to baseline** — 4.78 vs 8.34 (43% better)
5. **Best diffusion setting is now η=0.3**: Mean RPA gap to baseline narrowed to only 2.9%

